# program: ../apps/window-designer/src/main.nx
# Window Designer, used the normal way: a window with a heading, a text
# field, a row with two buttons, a list and a check box; moved around,
# seen in the preview and as code, exported and copied. After a part is
# added its words are typed straight away; Enter goes back to the parts.
file Documents/readme.txt my documents
window Window Designer
shot empty
key shift+Tab shift+Tab ctrl+a
type Notes
key Tab ctrl+a
type notes-app
# into the parts list: Heading is picked; Enter adds it
key Tab Return
type My notes
key Return Down Down Down Down Down Return
type Write a note
key Return Down Down Down Return
key Up Up Up Up Up Return
type Clear
key Return Down Return
type Add note
key Return
# the main button goes first in its row; a list after the row
key alt+Up
key Down Down Down Return
key alt+Left
type No notes yet. Write one above and press Add note.
key Return Up Return
type Keep them "sorted" {by date}
key Tab space
# a second main button is refused
key shift+Tab shift+Tab shift+Tab Up Up Return
shot editing
key F5
shot preview
key ctrl+shift+F12
key F5
key F6
shot code
key F6
key ctrl+e
window Export the program
shot export
key Return
gone Export the program
window Window Designer
shot exported
key ctrl+shift+F12
key Escape
show Documents/notes-app.nx
show .local/share/window-designer/design.json
